               "fundamental":  "Amazon\u0027s Q3 2026 results (Oct 29) reinforced its cloud-ecosystem moat even as spending pressured cash flow. Total revenue rose 12% YoY to $201.9B with a record 13.9% operating margin ($28.1B), powered by AWS\u0027s 39.3% surge to $46.0B ($184B annualized run rate) and a $578B backlog. AI demand is scaling rapidly: Bedrock token volume grew nearly 17x YoY, while Trainium and Graviton commitments jumped over 20x. Anthropic\u0027s Nov 19 IPO ($1.5T valuation) crystallized Amazon\u0027s 14.7% stake alongside $110B+ in AWS compute commitments, and the Nov 23 reported $7.5B Decart optimization deal strengthens AWS\u0027s push to sell Trainium externally. However, funding ~$220B in 2026 CapEx pushed trailing free cash flow to -$42.4B, keeping near-term sentiment cautious despite healthy Q4 guidance ($240B–$247B sales; $28.5B–$33.5B operating income).",
