               "summary":  "AMZN closed at $255.39 on Nov 23, 2026 (+3.47%), rebounding on Amazon\u0027s reported $7.5B deal for Decart\u0027s AI optimization stack and Anthropic\u0027s Nov 19 IPO, which showcased Amazon\u0027s 14.7% stake and $110B+ AWS compute commitments. On Oct 29, Q3 AWS sales jumped 39.3% YoY to $46.0B with a $578B backlog, confirming Amazon\u0027s cloud moat. Yet shares remain 11.1% below their $287.20 52-week high as ~$220B in 2026 CapEx pushed trailing free cash flow to -$42.4B. Technically, AMZN sits in neutral consolidation just below its EMA 50 ($256.62) on average volume.",
               "technical":  "As of Nov 23, 2026, AMZN exhibits a neutral consolidation within a still-intact long-term uptrend. Price closed at $255.39 (+3.47%), sitting between its EMA 50 ($256.62) and EMA 100 ($254.18)—exponential moving averages that track medium-term trends—while holding 3.0% above its long-term EMA 200 ($247.94). Because EMA 50 \u003e EMA 100 \u003e EMA 200, the primary trend remains constructive, though intraday selling pulled shares back from $262.48. Momentum is muted: RSI 14—a 0–100 momentum gauge where under 30 is oversold and over 70 is overbought—reads a neutral 48.44. MACD—a trend-momentum gauge comparing fast and slow averages—is positive at 0.59 but below its 1.71 signal line (histogram -1.12), reflecting lingering pullback pressure. In Bollinger Bands—a 20-day volatility envelope ($240.25–$275.22)—price sits just under the $257.74 midline and 11.1% below its $287.20 52-week high (vs $196.00 low). Volume of 53.17M slightly trailed the 54.00M 20-day average, showing limited breakout conviction. Key resistance sits at $256.62–$262.48, with support near $254.18 and $247.94."
